      "ms": 1152,
      "raw": "I disagree with the claim that React is always better than Vue. React’s flexibility and massive ecosystem make it a strong choice for large, highly customizable applications, but that same flexibility can add complexity and boilerplate. Vue, on the other hand, offers a more opinionated structure, clearer defaults, and a gentler learning curve, which often leads to faster development for smaller to medium‑scale projects. Performance differences are negligible in most real‑world scenarios; the deciding factor tends to be team familiarity, project requirements, and the specific tooling each framework provides. \n\nBoth frameworks excel in different contexts, so saying one is universally superior oversimplifies the trade‑offs.",
