      "raw": "\"Always\" is the wrong word. It makes the claim unfalsifiable.\n\nReact wins on ecosystem, hiring pool, and the mental model of \"it's just JavaScript.\" If you're building something that needs every niche library, or you're staffing a large team from the general market, React is the pragmatic choice.\n\nVue wins on ergonomics out of the box: single-file components, built-in reactivity without dependency arrays, `<script setup>` with TypeScript that actually feels good, first-party router and pinia that don't require evaluating five competing options. The learning curve is genuinely lower, and the DX stays consistent as the app grows.\n\nNeither is universally better. The honest answer is \"it depends on the team, the project, and what you're optimizing for.\"\n\nWhat made you land hard on React?",
